{title: Like a Weaned Child}
{subtitle: Psalm 131}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Ab] | [Bb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [Eb]Lord, my heart is not [Gm7]lifted up
My [Ab]eyes are not raised [Bb]too high
I [Eb]do not occupy myself [Gm7]with things
Too [Ab]great and too [Bb]marvelous for me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [Eb]calmed and quieted my [Bb]soul
Like a weaned [Cm]child with its moth[Ab]er
Like a [Eb]weaned [Bb]child
Is my [Ab]soul within me
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Ab] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O [Eb]Israel, hope [Gm7]in the Lord
From [Ab]this time forth and fo[Bb]revermore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [Eb]calmed and quieted [Bb]my soul
Like a [Cm]weaned child with its [Ab]mother
Like [Eb]a weaned [Bb]child
Is my [Ab]soul within me
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Ab] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] |
